  <string name="analyze_info">Q is the expected result of the hand, in points, against three players like the network. The list holds the arrangements no other arrangement beats in every row, best Q first; tap one for its cards and the network\'s probabilities. Your arrangement, when the hand comes from a game, is pinned on top; its numbers that differ notably from the best arrangement\'s are green where it does better and red where it does worse. The rules are shown above the list; under rules where special rows pay only when they win, the chances that an opponent\'s special row beats yours are listed too. Above the list are short remarks: what yours could do better, only when it is clearly worse (the network is not exact, so a small gap means as good); what kind of choice the best one is against the best of other row types (attacking: more scoops and more scooped; defensive: fewer of both; under row scoring, rows or scoops first); and the names of common arrangements, such as five pairs.</string>
